<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <!-- Package Information -->
    <id>egovframe</id>
    <version>4.3.1</version>
    <title>eGovFrameWork</title>
    <authors>leejongyoung</authors>
    <owners>egovframe</owners>
    <projectUrl>https://egovframe.go.kr</projectUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://egovframe.go.kr/statics/rebuild/images/logo.png</iconUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>true</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <tags>egovframe java spring framework</tags>
    
    <!-- Description -->
    <summary>eGovFrame is a public software development framework used in South Korea.</summary>
    <description>
      eGovFrame (Electronic Government Framework) is the standard framework for public sector application development in South Korea.

      ### [Components]
      The Development Environment for Windows 64-bit (Implementation Tool) Version 4.3.1 is a toolset that supports developers in writing code. It includes an IDE and editors for eGovFrame-based application development (SourceCode, UML, ERD, DBIO, WebFlow, Code Generation, Code Inspection, Common Component Wizard, Customized Dev Environment, Nexus, SVN), as well as Debug (Local, Remote), Mobile IDE, Batch IDE, and RTE.

      ### [Installation and Usage]
      - This package installs automatically to `C:\Program Files\eGovFrame`.
      - Launch the `eclipse` shortcut created on the Desktop.
      - Verify the `eclipse` folder and `workspace-egov` folder inside `eGovFrameDev-4.3.1-64bit`.
      - After launching `eclipse.exe`, confirm the `workspace-egov` path is correct and click Launch.

      ### [Troubleshooting]
      1. **JVM error**: You may need to set the JDK 17 path in `eclipse.ini`. (JDK 17 required)
         Example: `-vm C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-17.x.x\bin\javaw.exe`
      2. **Garbled characters**: Add `-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8` to `eclipse.ini` to set the Eclipse file encoding to UTF-8.
      3. **Garbled characters in template DML**: Change the encoding of the affected DML file to EUC-KR to resolve the issue.

      **Note: This package only supports 64-bit Windows systems.**
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>
      ### [Improvements]

      #### 1. Version 4.3.1
      - Applied Common Component 4.3.1 security patch
      - Pinned Spring Framework version to 5.3.37 for Boot Board, Boot Template, MSA Template, and Batch Template
      - Updated dependencies for the Common Component Creation Wizard

      #### 2. Version 4.3.0
      - Applied Eclipse 2024-03 (4.31.0)
      - Applied Runtime Environment 4.3.0
      - Upgraded 254 Common Components and applied security patches
      - Upgraded Template Projects (3 types), Batch Template, Boot Template, MSA Template, and more
      - Updated and added XML and Java Config configuration file generation features
      - Added Properties and YAML support for Logging configuration file generation
    </releaseNotes>

    <!-- Package Source URL -->
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/leejongyoung/egovframe-chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    
    <!-- Optional Information -->
    <docsUrl>https://www.egovframe.go.kr/wiki</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://www.egovframe.go.kr/home/sub.do?menuNo=69</bugTrackerUrl>
    
    <!-- Dependencies -->
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="openjdk" version="[17,)" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <files>
